{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523375-rank-6-rites","id":1523375,"title":"Rank 6 Rites?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-30T16:06:10-07:00","id":1523375,"title":"Rank 6 Rites?","content":"During my research i've heard there's rank 6 rites. How is that possible since Garou cannot get to ritual 6, a prerequisite for learning and parcticing those ritual. And what are those rank 6 rites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T16:40:48-07:00","id":1523378,"title":"","content":"One was passed down among Mound Builder kin of Middle Brother who revered both Luna and Helios. It allowed them to call the sun back over the horizon at night. It required a much more extensive ceremony and set of preparations than a typical rite, though given the nigh-legendary difficult that the rite of caern building, it'd have to be quite extensive indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T03:03:40-07:00","id":1523401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523375-rank-6-rites#post1523375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">During my research i've heard there's rank 6 rites. How is that possible since Garou cannot get to ritual 6, a prerequisite for learning and parcticing those ritual. And what are those rank 6 rites?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think that you need Rituals 6 to know a Level 6 Ritual?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T14:18:49-07:00","id":1523440,"title":"","content":"In every edition of the corebook (1e, 2e, Rev, W20), the description of the Rituals ability says some version of &quot;A character cannot learn a rite of higher level than his Rituals rating.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now I don't know any of the rules associated with Legendary (Rank 6) characters, so I don't know if they actually allow such characters to improve their traits beyond 5. If they don't, this is likely just some oversight. If so, I'd let such characters learn and perform such rituals even at Rituals 5 with the thought being the Rank itself fulfills any criteria.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T16:32:51-07:00","id":1523442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523375-rank-6-rites?p=1523440#post1523440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In every edition of the corebook (1e, 2e, Rev, W20), the description of the Rituals ability says some version of &quot;A character cannot learn a rite of higher level than his Rituals rating.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now I don't know any of the rules associated with Legendary (Rank 6) characters, so I don't know if they actually allow such characters to improve their traits beyond 5. If they don't, this is likely just some oversight. If so, I'd let such characters learn and perform such rituals even at Rituals 5 with the thought being the Rank itself fulfills any criteria.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Black fox told in w20 it is told in the rite background p.141, and in the description of the rites learning p.203 that you need to have the same level of ritual knowledge than the rite you want to learn, that's why it seems strange that level 6 rituals exist since Garou cannot get to level 6 in their caracteristics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T17:23:22-07:00","id":1523443,"title":"","content":"Any published Level Six rites were likely published separately in only a few sourcebooks. Like anything having to do with Legendary Rank, they are likely less handled by game mechanics and more about ST discretion about whatever story is being built around it. They are meant to be the conclusion of epic quests by only the mightiest heroes whose names will be forever remembered in Garou legend. If the character is not akin to Heracles, Beowulf, Galahad, the Hero Twins, and so on, they're just not capable of performing the rite successfully.<br /> <br /> There is a previous post on this forum listing all the level six rites one poster could find. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1409472-all-level-6-rites-and-their-resources\">That thread is located here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T17:30:01-07:00","id":1523445,"title":"","content":"Good to know as always <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-01T20:34:19-07:00","id":1523451,"title":"","content":"Legendary/Rank 6 Rites were one of those things that just kinda got added to the game without ever being fully considered.<br /> <br /> That said, the way Rank 6 Gifts work seems apropos: There is no such think as a Rank 6 Garou, in-character or mechanically (so if a Gift uses Rank in its math, a Legendary Garou is still Rank 5). Legendary Garou are Elders that have reach such esteem and accomplishment than they get extra perks like access to Rank 6 Gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T08:17:05-07:00","id":1523466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523375-rank-6-rites?p=1523451#post1523451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legendary/Rank 6 Rites were one of those things that just kinda got added to the game without ever being fully considered.<br /> <br /> That said, the way Rank 6 Gifts work seems apropos: There is no such think as a Rank 6 Garou, in-character or mechanically (so if a Gift uses Rank in its math, a Legendary Garou is still Rank 5). Legendary Garou are Elders that have reach such esteem and accomplishment than they get extra perks like access to Rank 6 Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying that technically the rank 6 rites are just said rank 6 because they are secret kept by legendary werewolf, right? So technically if a werewolf with ritual 5 achieve to learn those secrets he can achieve a rank 6 gift. I admit that it make sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-02T12:15:21-07:00","id":1523470,"title":"","content":"I never said anything about them being kept secret by Garou of high Rank.<br /> <br /> They're Legendary because they're legends. They're rites of such ridiculous difficulty and power that pulling them off is beyond the majority of Garou that have ever lived even if they learned everything to learn about them as Cubs. They're only used in the most dire of dire-circumstances that require the mobilization of large numbers of people to get everything in place.<br /> <br /> The two ones listed in the other thread don't have real systems involved, because they're plot devices, not things the PCs are ever expected to enact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T02:27:59-07:00","id":1523488,"title":"","content":"It's a bit disappointing those rank 6 are only plot device, a theurge pc specialised in rituals could be frustrated knowing that only getting to rank 6 could take years of game and that even if they finally succeed there's no way for them to perform those kind of rite.<br /> <br /> Too bad, maybe rank 6 is to powerful to be played by a pc after all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-03T12:43:06-07:00","id":1523507,"title":"","content":"Eh? Given that Rank isn't directly tied to Rites like that, I don't see the problem. Rite-master style PCs that made it to Rank 5 weren't disappointing before Legendary Status and Rank 6 Gifts were officially a thing. Those were added to the game later (largely because 2e WoD had a lot of problems with writers thinking non-vampires went over 5 in things that didn't inherently go over 5 and gave NPCs 6s without anyone catching it and then late 2e/Rev. decided to incorporate the ideas into the games because players liked it).<br /> <br /> And even then the Rank 6 Gifts are pretty underwhelming (at lot of them are also just plot devices too). Becoming a Garou legend is the fun part. It's not supposed to be some win-state where you suddenly have &quot;I Win&quot; powers. Garou become Legendary by having power and winning in the first place, they stuff they get isn't really about making them more powerful, it's about giving them signature powers that make them standout uniquely (not necessarily more powerfully) than normal Elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T09:54:57-07:00","id":1523560,"title":"","content":"It's true that some rank 6 gifts are not that powerfull, in fact some of my friends have already pointed in the past that some gift are too powerfull for their rank and some other on the other hand not enough. But as all gift are different in their effect It's almost impossible to avoid that, Discipline powers can be sorted by level because they only target one kind of effect each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T13:52:23-07:00","id":1523572,"title":"","content":"You're... skipping the point. The Rank 6 Gifts aren't meant to be major power increases over lower Rank Gifts like 6+ Discipline dot powers are. They're meant to be plot devices that give Legendary Garou that ability to do things well beyond the norm to fulfill a specific purpose. Jonas's Rank 6 Gift exists because it's the only way for him to defeat Zhyzhak: force her into a one-on-one duel and remove the numerical advantage she has as the leader of a massive Wyrm army that's largely held together by her iron hand. The ability to force an opponent into a one-on-one duel isn't, by itself, all that special. But it's an essential part of the plot of Jonas's story that he has the weird unique power to turn the tides of the War at the most crucial moment.<br /> <br /> While it's worth looking at the mechanics of some of the Rank 6 Gifts because with so many Gifts there are few that are kinda silly (as in they aren't unique special powers, they're just more expensive versions of Gifts that already exist at Rank 5), in general analyzing them by &quot;power balance&quot; isn't going to work because they don't exist for that context. They exist to generate specific plot events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T16:14:59-07:00","id":1523581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523375-rank-6-rites?p=1523572#post1523572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're... skipping the point. The Rank 6 Gifts aren't meant to be major power increases over lower Rank Gifts like 6+ Discipline dot powers are. They're meant to be plot devices that give Legendary Garou that ability to do things well beyond the norm to fulfill a specific purpose. Jonas's Rank 6 Gift exists because it's the only way for him to defeat Zhyzhak: force her into a one-on-one duel and remove the numerical advantage she has as the leader of a massive Wyrm army that's largely held together by her iron hand. The ability to force an opponent into a one-on-one duel isn't, by itself, all that special. But it's an essential part of the plot of Jonas's story that he has the weird unique power to turn the tides of the War at the most crucial moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... of course i missed the point, those informations aren't in the core book, the only information i know about Zyzhak is in the book of the wyrm where it is said that she is supposed to destroy the last garou great hero during the apocalypse. That rank 6 gift you're talking to force a 1 on 1 fight isn't even in the books i have, nore are those information about Jonas. All we have are the few listed in W20 with only their effect description and system. The rank 6 Arhoun &quot;Unstoppable Warrior&quot; also has this plot use for a specific character? So is the theurge one &quot;As in the Beggining&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T21:19:56-07:00","id":1523755,"title":"","content":"lv6 Rites: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1409472-all-level-6-rites-and-their-resources\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...heir-resources</a><br /> <br /> Gifts: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1395272-all-rank-6-gifts-and-their-resources\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...heir-resources</a><br /> <br /> Fetishes: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1407885-all-level-6-fetishes-and-their-resources\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...heir-resources</a><br /> <br /> NPCs: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1408866-all-rank-6-shapechangers-and-their-resources\">https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/...heir-resources</a><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T18:42:31-07:00","id":1523852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523375-rank-6-rites?p=1523440#post1523440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In every edition of the corebook (1e, 2e, Rev, W20), the description of the Rituals ability says some version of &quot;A character cannot learn a rite of higher level than his Rituals rating.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now I don't know any of the rules associated with Legendary (Rank 6) characters, so I don't know if they actually allow such characters to improve their traits beyond 5. If they don't, this is likely just some oversight. If so, I'd let such characters learn and perform such rituals even at Rituals 5 with the thought being the Rank itself fulfills any criteria.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. But just like Rank 6 is not mechanically defined so the Level 6 Rites are outside the mechanical constraints. They're here to serve narrative purposes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}